  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Service-Disabled Veteran-Owned Small Business Set-Aside Federal Contracts obligated $6.3B in FY2026 to date. The program recorded 12,644 awards with an average award size of $496K, and obligations fell 27.8% year over year. Year-to-year totals show a peak in FY23 at $9.1B followed by declines to $8.8B in FY24, $8.7B in FY25, and the current FY26 total of $6.3B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer with $5B in obligations, while the Department of Defense is the second-largest buyer at $641M. Construction and IT dominate the industry mix, led by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $1.8B and Other Computer Related Services at $1.3B. Top vendor concentration is visible: V3GATE, LLC leads vendors with $350M, followed by FOUR POINTS TECHNOLOGY, L.L.C. at $254M and SPREZZATURA MANAGEMENT CONSULTING, LLC at $214M. This snapshot covers fiscal year to date obligations and reflects partial current-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did obligations change compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations for Service-Disabled Veteran-Owned Small Business Set-Aside Federal Contracts fell 27.8% year over year. Annual obligations rose from $7.2B in FY21 to $9.1B in FY23, then declined to $8.8B in FY24 and $8.7B in FY25 before landing at $6.3B in FY26 to date. The current-year total is a fiscal year to date figure and therefore partial. Watch whether the remainder of FY2026 narrows or widens the gap versus prior years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries lead SDVOSB set-aside obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $5B, making it the largest buyer in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $641M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $120M. V3GATE, LLC is the largest vendor at $350M, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction leads industries at $1.8B, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $1.3B."
      }
    ]
  },
